.TH SECRETARY 1 "2026-08-12" "secretary 0.1.0" "Secretary CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
secretary \- atomic, deterministic operations for the secretary personal-assistant engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B secretary
[\fB\-\-version\fR|\fB\-V\fR]
.br
.B secretary
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fISUBCOMMAND\fR] [\fIARGS\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B secretary
is the deterministic, scriptable command layer of the secretary engine. It resolves
paths, posts status, runs validators, searches memory, and performs other mechanical
operations without invoking an LLM. Agentic judgment and synthesis live in separate
.B sec-*
skills, which call into
.B secretary
for path resolution and other primitives.
.PP
.B secretary
reads a private
.I instance
directory, selected by the
.B SECRETARY_INSTANCE
environment variable (default
.IR ~/.secretary ),
and its
.I .secretary.yml
configuration file. The engine source tree itself is located via
.B SECRETARY_CORE
when running uninstalled.
.PP
Commands are organized as a tree of command groups (Typer/Click sub-apps). Run
.B secretary \-\-help
or
.B secretary \fICOMMAND\fR \-\-help
at any level for the authoritative, live list of commands and options.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-V
Print the installed
.B secretary
version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SECRETARY_INSTANCE
Path to the instance data root: config (
.IR .secretary.yml ),
extractors, and memory. Defaults to
.IR ~/.secretary .
.TP
.B SECRETARY_CORE
Path to the secretary-core engine checkout (wiki build engine, shared code). Needed
when running uninstalled via
.IR "python3 \-m secretary.main" .
.SH COMMANDS
.SS secretary env
Emit shell exports for instance bootstrap. Intended for
.IR "eval \[dq]$(secretary env)\[dq]" .
Prints
.IR "export SECRETARY_INSTANCE=\[dq]...\[dq]" .
.SS secretary menu
Launch the interactive guided menu (questionary-based TUI) for common operations.
.SS secretary paths
List all configured extractor/wiki path keys, their resolved absolute paths, and
whether each currently exists.
.SS secretary status \fIEMOJI\fR \fIREF\fR \fINOTE\fR
Persist progress on today's brief (atomic sec-status).
.TP
.I EMOJI
One of \[dq]\[u2705]\[dq] (done), \[dq]\[u1F504]\[dq] (in progress), \[dq]\[u23F3]\[dq] (waiting), \[dq]\[u1F6AB]\[dq] (blocked).
.TP
.I REF
A brief item reference (\fI#N\fR) or an action-ledger id; empty string if not applicable.
.TP
.I NOTE
Free-text progress note.
.SS "secretary validate [TARGET]"
Run instance CI validators from
.IR scripts/ci/ .
.I TARGET
is an optional validator name; omit to run all validators.
.SS secretary fresh \fIMODULE\fR [\fB\-\-format\fR|\fB\-f\fR \fIFMT\fR] [\fB\-\-local\fR]
Paso 0 fresh-first check \(em confirms
.IR main ,
open auto-PRs, and live source state for an extractor before acting on it.
.TP
.I MODULE
One of: \fImail\fR, \fImeeting\fR, \fIreuniones\fR, \fIdrive\fR, \fIwhatsapp\fR, \fIall\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-format ", " \-f " " \fIFMT\fR
Output format: \fItable\fR (default), \fIjson\fR, or \fImarkdown\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-local
Include the working-tree diff against \fIorigin/main\fR.
.SS secretary recall \fIQUERY\fR [\fB\-\-format\fR|\fB\-f\fR \fIFMT\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIN\fR]
Deterministic memory search (sec-recall step 0): greps wiki articles and module memory
for
.IR QUERY .
.TP
.BR \-\-format ", " \-f " " \fIFMT\fR
Output format: \fItable\fR (default) or \fIjson\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-limit \fIN\fR
Maximum number of hits to return (default 40).
.SS secretary config
Instance config and path resolution.
.TP
.B secretary config show [\fB\-\-yaml\fR]
Dump the resolved instance config with all paths made absolute. JSON by default;
.B \-\-yaml
emits raw YAML instead.
.TP
.B secretary config path \fIKEY\fR
Resolve a dotted config key (e.g. \fImail.memory\fR) to an absolute filesystem path.
.SS secretary dispatch
dispatch.executor allowlist operations (no LLM).
.TP
.B secretary dispatch locate [\fICWD\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR|\fB\-f\fR \fIFMT\fR]
Match a directory against
.I dispatch.executor.repos
in
.IR .secretary.yml .
.I CWD
defaults to the process working directory. Exits 0 with the matching repo(s) on
stdout (deepest path first), or exits 1 with empty stdout when no entry matches.
Replaces the jq-based bash loop formerly used by the sec-drone skill.
.TP
.BR \-\-format ", " \-f " " \fIFMT\fR
Output format: \fItable\fR (default) or \fIjson\fR.
.SS secretary wiki
Wiki build and related operations.
.TP
.B secretary wiki build
Build the wiki HTML via the engine's
.I build.py
using a staged instance layout (temporary directory of symlinks mapping the
instance's
.I memoria/wiki/
and
.I extractores/
into the legacy top-level names
.I build.py
expects). Does not mutate the instance.
.TP
.B secretary wiki serve [\fB\-\-port\fR \fIN\fR]
Serve the generated wiki HTML. Default port 8123.
.SS secretary acc
Action ledger operations.
.TP
.B secretary acc fold \fIACC_ID\fR \fIEVIDENCIA\fR [\fICERRADO\fR]
Fold a canonical action closure into
.IR acciones.md .
.I ACC_ID
has the form
.IR acc\-YYYYMMDD\-NNN .
.I EVIDENCIA
is closure evidence, e.g.
.IR pr:owner/repo#N .
.I CERRADO
is an optional close date
.RI ( YYYY\-MM\-DD ),
defaulting to today.
.SS secretary routines
Scheduled routines router and LaunchAgent setup.
.TP
.B secretary routines setup
Interactive wizard to configure
.I dispatch.routines
router
.RI ( claude\-scheduled ", " cursor\-cron ", or " api\-cron ),
per-routine enable/disable, required
.I .env
keys,
.IR install\-routine\-schedule.sh ,
and LaunchAgent reload.
.SS secretary modules
Module contracts and health.
.TP
.B secretary modules list [\fB\-\-format\fR|\fB\-f\fR \fIFMT\fR]
List extractors and loops with contract metadata (id, plane, kind, routine).
.TP
.B secretary modules health [\fB\-\-module\fR|\fB\-m\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR|\fB\-f\fR \fIFMT\fR]
Audit contract freshness and loop success criteria across modules, or for a single
module when
.B \-\-module
is given.
.TP
.B secretary modules contract get \fIMODULE_ID\fR [\fB\-\-format\fR|\fB\-f\fR \fIFMT\fR]
Return the full
.I contract.yaml
for a module. Default format is \fIjson\fR.
.TP
.B secretary modules contract put \fIMODULE_ID\fR [\fB\-\-file\fR \fIPATCH_FILE\fR]
Admin update: shallow-merge a YAML/JSON patch file into a module's
.I contract.yaml
(human gate \(em no LLM writes).
.SS secretary dream
sec-dream deterministic collection.
.TP
.B secretary dream collect [\fB\-\-write\-collect\fR]
Run the instance's deterministic sec-dream Phase 1 gather
.RI ( scripts/dream/collect.py ).
.B \-\-write\-collect
also writes a
.I collect/
snapshot (gitignored).
.TP
.B secretary dream emit\-metrics [\fB\-\-since\fR \fIISO_DATE\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
Append the current sec-dream run to
.I metrics.jsonl
via the Claude-scheduled session backfill.
.B \-\-since
sets the ISO date (Lima time) to search from, default today.
.SS secretary portal
Operator portal.
.TP
.B secretary portal aggregate [\fB\-\-output\fR|\fB\-o\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-stdout\fR] [\fB\-\-validate\-only\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-serve\fR] [\fB\-\-port\fR \fIN\fR]
Generate a portal snapshot via the instance's
.IR scripts/portal/aggregate.py .
Default output is
.IR subsystem/portal/live\-data.json .
.B \-\-serve
starts a static server exposing
.I POST /api/refresh
on
.B \-\-port
(default 8765).
.B \-\-validate\-only
validates an existing JSON file against the schema instead of generating one.
.SS secretary core
Engine maintenance operations.
.TP
.B secretary core export\-examples [\fB\-\-check\fR]
Regenerate
.I playbooks.example/
and
.I skills.example/
from the private
.I playbooks/
and
.I skills/
directories, applying the anonymization map. Never writes
.IR docs/ ,
.IR README.md ,
.IR CLAUDE.md ,
.IR AGENTS.md ,
or
.IR CONTRIBUTING.md .
Exits 2 if a real source directory is missing.
.B \-\-check
regenerates into a temporary directory and diffs against the committed
.I .example
directories instead of writing, failing on any drift (CI / pre-commit gate).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Command-specific failure (e.g.
.I dispatch locate
found no matching repo).
.TP
.B 2
Precondition failure (e.g.
.I core export\-examples
missing a required private source directory).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .secretary.yml
Instance configuration: path keys, dispatch executor allowlist, routines router.
.TP
.I $SECRETARY_INSTANCE
Instance data root (default
.IR ~/.secretary ).
.TP
.I $SECRETARY_CORE/secretary/
CLI source (Typer application, entry point
.IR secretary.main:app ).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Bootstrap a shell with the instance path:
.B eval "$(secretary env)"
.TP
List all resolved paths:
.B secretary paths
.TP
Search memory for a topic, as JSON:
.B secretary recall "acme renewal" \-\-format json
.TP
Check whether the current directory has a dispatch target:
.B secretary dispatch locate
.TP
Run every CI validator:
.B secretary validate
.TP
Fold a closed action into the ledger:
.B secretary acc fold acc\-20260812\-001 pr:owner/repo#42
.SH SEE ALSO
.I cli/README.md
and
.I CLAUDE.md
in the secretary-core repository; run
.B secretary \-\-help
or
.B secretary \fICOMMAND\fR \-\-help
for live, authoritative usage.
